node_modules/
_build/
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.log
*.out
.vigiles/state/

# 🔴 The pipeline's reproduction logs are EVIDENCE, not build output. `*.log` above is a LaTeX rule
# (`paper.log`), and it silently swallowed all 13 files under skills/paper-pipeline/repro/ when they
# arrived — a commit would have carried the eval claims and none of the raw runs behind them, which is
# the exact artifact loss `repro/` exists to prevent. Measured at the moment of the move, not guessed:
# `git check-ignore -v` named this line for every one of them.
!skills/paper-pipeline/repro/*.log

# Mutex for run exclusivity (scripts/exclusive.mjs) — exists only during a run.
.vigiles/exclusive.lock/
dist/

# Runtime decision log written by the vigiles hook runner on every deny. It records what
# happened on THIS machine during THIS run, so it is telemetry, not evidence: committing it
# would replay one developer's local probe as if it were a property of the package.
.vigiles/runs.jsonl

# What a LOCAL `vigiles test` run exercised. Never committed: it describes this checkout at this
# moment, and a committed copy credits coverage on a machine where nothing ran (vigiles'
# docs/rules/untested-skill.md says so, and vigiles ignores it in its own repository). Measured
# 2026-09-23 before untracking: nothing here read it, its one record had not changed since
# 2026-09-12, and each of its last five commits changed only the `generated`/`commit` stamps.
.vigiles/coverage.json
